The Studio half of Phase 0. No new environment is visible yet; what lands
is the layer every environment will be a renderer over, wired into the
shell without changing what any existing panel does.

  · Programming mode — lib/programmingMode.ts + ModeContext: studio | grid |
    architect | flow | intelligent, resolved URL → memory → default, with an
    unavailable mode falling back rather than opening on nothing. A selector
    in the top bar shows all five; the four without a renderer are disabled
    with their tagline. Switching is a state change: no reload, no refetch,
    `?mode=` kept in step with replaceState.

  · One selection — lib/selection.ts (a pure reducer: select / toggle /
    shift-range / set / drop) + SelectionContext, keyed by the engine's
    ObjectKey so a grid row, a flow node and a display rule are the same
    kind of thing. The store's `selectedQuestionId` is now a mirror of the
    question primary, in both directions, so every panel and browser suite
    that reads it is untouched.

  · Commands — lib/commands/core.ts (types, shortcut parsing, fuzzy ranking,
    applicability) and builtins.ts (add question / block / branch /
    randomizer / loop / quota check / embedded data / display rule /
    calculation, duplicate, move, undo/redo, save, test, preview, one
    "Open <tab>" per tab, and object finders for questions, calcs and
    rules). Each calls the same engine function the panel button calls.
    CommandContext is the one keyboard handler: a chord fires only when its
    command applies and never while typing unless marked global (⌘K, ⌘S).
    Shortcuts that browsers own (⌘1–9, ⌘⇧N, ⌘⇧T) were deliberately avoided.

  · ⌘K — CommandPalette: empty query lists applicable commands grouped;
    typing ranks commands and survey objects together, so "Q14" jumps to
    Q14 and "adq" offers Add question. ↑ ↓ Enter Esc; a top-bar button for
    people who do not know the key.

  · Flow node defaults moved from FlowPanel to blockModel.newFlowNode so
    the palette inserts exactly the node the panel would.

Found along the way and fixed: PropertiesPanel called two hooks after its
early returns, so every select/deselect logged React's hooks-order warning;
hoisted. scripts/test-survey-sync-test.mjs still asserted the `?v=` pin and
the "please retry" toast that the live-sync and save-flow fixes removed;
brought up to the current contracts.

